{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1523514-coming-from-1e-and-finally-looking-over-my-books-and-now-have-some-questions","id":1523514,"title":"Coming from 1e and Finally looking over my books...and now have some questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-03T15:28:55-07:00","id":1523514,"title":"Coming from 1e and Finally looking over my books...and now have some questions","content":"So I am an old Eon-ite finally getting around to reading everything around Aberrant in the new generation. I am getting through the books and am wondering a few things.<br /> <br /> 1. Why is Cestus Pax a sympathetic hero now, rather then a butthead anti-hero? In the prior edition he he still had his &quot;strongest&quot; Nova role, but that strength came tainted. He had multiple aberrations (perfect looks and narcissism in particular) that were built in. Considering how transcendence is very very much &quot;you cant go back&quot; now, I dont know why that wouldn't come over to the new edition for someone who erupted 40 years before everyone else and is in a position where he has probably had to push himself many times to advance without knowledge of how to mitigate. It does not seem to mesh.<br /> <br /> 2. I haven't seen anything about the sterility cocktail in the book so far, so it seems like that plot point was dropped since Proteus are now part of the 'good guys'. Have I over looked 2nd gen nova kids somewhere? I do tend to skip around RPG books so I may have missed things. I would have thought there would be *some* mention of them somewhere.<br /> <br /> 3. Is there any mention of adrenacilin and mox anywhere? Mox in particular was a stable of the older game as something that helped newly erupted novas so it seems strange they would drop it even if they removed the sterility cocktail stuff.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25366-bahamut810","name":"Bahamut810","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T17:24:53-07:00","id":1523517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bahamut810</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1523514-coming-from-1e-and-finally-looking-over-my-books-and-now-have-some-questions#post1523514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am an old Eon-ite finally getting around to reading everything around Aberrant in the new generation. I am getting through the books and am wondering a few things.<br /> <br /> 1. Why is Cestus Pax a sympathetic hero now, rather then a butthead anti-hero? In the prior edition he he still had his &quot;strongest&quot; Nova role, but that strength came tainted. He had multiple aberrations (perfect looks and narcissism in particular) that were built in. Considering how transcendence is very very much &quot;you cant go back&quot; now, I dont know why that wouldn't come over to the new edition for someone who erupted 40 years before everyone else and is in a position where he has probably had to push himself many times to advance without knowledge of how to mitigate. It does not seem to mesh.<br /> <br /> 2. I haven't seen anything about the sterility cocktail in the book so far, so it seems like that plot point was dropped since Proteus are now part of the 'good guys'. Have I over looked 2nd gen nova kids somewhere? I do tend to skip around RPG books so I may have missed things. I would have thought there would be *some* mention of them somewhere.<br /> <br /> 3. Is there any mention of adrenacilin and mox anywhere? Mox in particular was a stable of the older game as something that helped newly erupted novas so it seems strange they would drop it even if they removed the sterility cocktail stuff.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really answer to the first question, being as I am not a line dev or the like. As for the second and third:<br /> <br /> 2. In 2e, Novas are now natively less fertile than baselines, with higher Quantum Ratings + Transcendence = higher sterility. So if you're tainted enough to look like Skeletor, it's very unlikely that you'll be having kids of your own outside of maybe cooking up a cloning vat or two, which isn't going to be reliable because of said taint. I thought this was stated in the book, but I can't seem to find it, so maybe it was just a Dev comment or is in one of the other books.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, they are both in the Technology section of the book under &quot;Bleeding Edge Design.&quot; No stats are given for what they do to Novas, but there is a sidebar for effects on baselines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T20:09:18-07:00","id":1523524,"title":"","content":"1. The idea here is kind of simple\u2026 The dev team decided to go for a more optimistic view, with Pax being a real hero, not a crazy butthead capable of leveling a city to show how powerful he is. That creates a team of Heroes that is good willed, not vengeful bastards or a team forced together by fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}